%% VM clear/set protocol: pin VM before locking heap (deadlock avoidance);
%% bit-set is LSN-aware; bit-clear is implicit in heap WAL.

sequenceDiagram
    participant Inserter
    participant VM as Visibility Map
    participant HeapPg as Heap page
    participant WAL
    participant Vacuum

    rect rgb(245,245,245)
    Note over Inserter: INSERT path (heap_insert)
    Inserter->>VM: visibilitymap_pin(blk)<br/>BEFORE heap-page lock
    Inserter->>HeapPg: LockBuffer(BUFFER_LOCK_EXCLUSIVE)
    Inserter->>HeapPg: insert tuple
    Inserter->>VM: visibilitymap_clear(blk)<br/>(if PD_ALL_VISIBLE was set)
    Inserter->>WAL: XLogInsert(XLOG_HEAP_INSERT)
    Note over WAL: clear is implicit in<br/>heap_xlog_insert redo
    end

    rect rgb(245,245,245)
    Note over Vacuum: VACUUM path
    Vacuum->>HeapPg: scan tuples,<br/>determine all-visible
    Vacuum->>WAL: XLogInsert(XLOG_HEAP2_VISIBLE)<br/>recptr = recptr_returned
    Vacuum->>VM: visibilitymap_set(blk, recptr,<br/>cutoff_xid, FLAGS)
    Note over VM: VM page LSN is updated<br/>to recptr (high-water mark);<br/>VM page LSN must not regress<br/>past youngest tuple it claims.
    end
